      "title": "[Five principal mountain chains of China]",
      "caption_extra": "With a general tendency of running from west to east, they may be grouped into five principal chains. These chains are:",
      "continued": false,
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": null,
          "columns": [
            "Chain",
            "Description"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "The Altai Range",
              "which forms the boundary mountains between China and the U. S. S. R."
            ],
            [
              "The Tienshan Range",
              "across the northern part of Sinkiang"
            ],
            [
              "The Kunlun Range",
              "which is again divided into several branches spreading out to Chinese provinces."
            ],
            [
              "The Trans-Himalaya Range",
              ""
            ],
            [
              "The Himalaya Range",
              ""
            ]
